     For each named _f_i_l_e, wwcc counts and prints the number of
     lines, words, and characters it contains.  A word is a maxi-
     mal run of characters delimited by a blank, a tab, or a
     newline; a line is counted at each newline character read.

     If no _f_i_l_e is named, wwcc reads the standard input and prints
     a single count with no file name attached.  If more than one
     _f_i_l_e is named, wwcc prints a count for each, in argument or-
     der, followed by a line labeled TToottaall that sums the counts
     over all of them.  A named file that cannot be opened is
     reported and skipped, and does not contribute to the total.

     -ll   Print only the line count.

     -ww   Print only the word count.

     -cc   Print only the character count.

     The -ll, -ww, and -cc options may be combined in one argument,
     e.g.  -llww prints both the line and word counts.  If none of
     them is given, wwcc prints all three counts, in the order
     lines, words, characters.

